{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6d96bb05-a4ed-4317-9e8a-ef818023debb",
    "name": "PropertyGpsApi - Single Plot GPS",
    "description": "BBMP Single Plot GPS backend.\n\nRun in order:\n1. Send OTP\n2. Verify OTP (paste the code; the token is saved automatically)\n3. Fetch applications\n\nIn Development no SMS is sent - the code is printed to the API console as \"DEV OTP for 9000000001 is 123456 (no SMS sent)\". You can also read it with:\n\n    SELECT TOP 1 OTP FROM OTP_Tran WHERE MobileNO = '9000000001' ORDER BY OTPID DESC;\n\nDo not retry with a wrong code: four failures deactivate the officer account.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "basePath",
      "value": "v1/api/gbagps/singlesite",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/live",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "live"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Process is up. Touches no dependencies."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Round-trips both databases with SELECT 1. Check this first if anything else fails."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Send OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"mobile\": \"{{mobile}}\",\n    \"deviceId\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/auth/otp/send",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Generates a six-digit code and stores it via USP_I_OTP.\n\nIn Development the response also carries \"devOtp\" - the code itself - and the test script saves it to {{otp}}, so Verify OTP needs no editing. That field is only ever populated when the Development sender is in use; a deployed instance cannot return it.\n\nRate limited to 5 per 5 minutes per IP."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('OTP sent', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "if (body.success && body.data && body.data.devOtp) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('otp', body.data.devOtp);",
                  "    console.log('OTP captured: ' + body.data.devOtp + ' - just run Verify OTP next.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No devOtp in the response. That means a real SMS was sent, so read the code from the phone.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"mobile\": \"{{mobile}}\",\n    \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\",\n    \"deviceId\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the code for a JWT.\n\nThe code comes from {{otp}}, which Send OTP filled in automatically. In production, replace it with the code from the SMS.\n\nOn success the token, corporationId, zoneId and wardId are saved to the environment.\n\nDo not retry with a wrong code: four failures deactivate the officer account."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('signed in', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "if (body.success && body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('token', body.data.token);",
                  "    if (body.data.corporationId) pm.environment.set('corporationId', String(body.data.corporationId));",
                  "    if (body.data.zoneId) pm.environment.set('zoneId', String(body.data.zoneId));",
                  "    if (body.data.wardId) pm.environment.set('wardId', String(body.data.wardId));",
                  "    console.log('Token saved to the environment.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No token. ' + body.code + ': ' + body.message);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Masters",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Zones for a corporation",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/masters/zones",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "masters",
                "zones"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Zones in a corporation. Needed because sign-in returns ward names but not ward ids."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Wards in a zone",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/masters/wards",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "masters",
                "wards"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wards in a zone, with the ids the fetch request needs."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Property info",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Fetch applications",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"corporationId\": \"{{corporationId}}\",\n    \"zoneId\": \"{{zoneId}}\",\n    \"wardId\": \"{{wardId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/propertyinfo/fetch",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "propertyinfo",
                "fetch"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The ward worklist the app caches in SQLite.\n\nThe officer and role come from the token, never the body. A role-116 officer asking for another ward gets 403 OUTSIDE_JURISDICTION.\n\nAdd an \"epid\" field to filter to one application."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
